# Stride — Cursor Project Rules

## What this project is
Stride is a personal marathon training dashboard for a single user. It replaces
Strava's paid analytics features (heatmaps, training load, route hotspots) with a
self-hosted app powered by the user's own Strava data, enriched with weather from
Open-Meteo, and an AI coaching layer via the Anthropic Claude API.

## Tech stack — never deviate from these without discussion
- **Framework**: Next.js 14 App Router (not Pages Router)
- **Language**: TypeScript — strict mode, no `any` types
- **Database**: Supabase (Postgres + PostGIS extension)
- **ORM**: Supabase JS client — no Prisma, no Drizzle
- **Maps**: Mapbox GL JS via react-map-gl
- **Charts**: Recharts
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS with CSS variables for the design system
- **Fonts**: Outfit (headings, logo, data values) + Plus Jakarta Sans (body)
- **AI**: Anthropic Claude API — model is always `claude-sonnet-4-20250514`
- **Deployment**: Vercel
- **CI/CD**: GitHub Actions

## Project structure
```
src/
  app/
    api/
      webhooks/strava/     — Strava webhook handler (GET verify + POST events)
      runs/                — Run CRUD endpoints
      ai/                  — AI insight endpoints
    dashboard/             — Home screen (calendar + stats)
    map/                   — Global heatmap screen
    training-load/         — CTL/ATL/TSB screen
    ai-insights/           — AI coaching panel
    race-predictor/        — Race time predictor
  components/
    ui/                    — Shared primitives (Card, Badge, Button, StatCard)
    calendar/              — TrainingCalendar, DayCell, RunDetailPanel
    map/                   — HeatmapLayer, HotspotPin, CityPanel
    charts/                — WeeklyMileageChart, TrainingLoadChart
    ai/                    — InsightCard, AnomalyFlag, WeatherCorrelation
  lib/
    strava/                — Strava OAuth, API client, webhook validation
    supabase/              — DB client, typed query helpers
    ai/                    — Claude API wrapper, prompt builders
    weather/               — Open-Meteo client
  types/                   — Shared TypeScript interfaces
  hooks/                   — Custom React hooks
supabase/
  migrations/              — SQL migration files (numbered, committed to repo)
```

## Design system — Chalk & Ember theme
See docs/DESIGN.md for full token reference. Key values:

```css
--bg: #FAF9F6;           /* off-white paper — page background */
--surface: #F0EDE6;      /* warm surface — card backgrounds */
--surface2: #E8E4DB;     /* deeper surface — inputs, mini-map bg */
--border: #DDD9D0;       /* default border */
--border2: #C8C3B8;      /* emphasis border */
--text: #1A1A1A;         /* primary text */
--text2: #6B6560;        /* secondary text */
--text3: #A09890;        /* muted/hint text */
--accent: #C0392B;       /* ember red — CTAs, active nav, highlights */
--accent2: #E74C3C;      /* lighter ember — hover states */
--easy: #2E7D32;         /* easy run colour */
--tempo: #B45309;        /* tempo run colour */
--long: #C0392B;         /* long run colour (same as accent) */
--race: #7C3AED;         /* race day colour */
```

Dark mode: warm brown darks, ember red accent preserved. Toggle via
`data-theme="dark"` on `<html>`. CSS variables shift automatically.

Font usage:
- `font-outfit` — logo, screen headings, stat values, nav items
- `font-jakarta` — body text, labels, descriptions, table content

## Database schema — key tables
See docs/SCHEMA.md for full reference.

```
runs          — strava_id, date, distance_m, duration_s, avg_hr, max_hr,
                elevation_m, polyline (TEXT), route (GEOMETRY LineString 4326),
                city, country, run_type (easy/tempo/long/race), tss, raw_json
laps          — run_id, lap_index, distance_m, elapsed_s, avg_hr, avg_pace_s
weather       — run_id, temp_c, humidity_pct, wind_kph, conditions, weather_code
ai_insights   — run_id (nullable), insight_type, prompt_hash, content,
                model, input_tokens, output_tokens, generated_at
settings      — singleton row: race_date, threshold_hr, threshold_pace_s,
                unit_preference (km/mi), strava_connected_at
```

## Environment variables
```
STRAVA_CLIENT_ID
STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET
STRAVA_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN
STRAVA_OWNER_ID
STRAVA_SUBSCRIPTION_ID
NEXT_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_TOKEN
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
```
Never hardcode these. Always read from `process.env`. Never expose
service role key to the client — only use it in server components and
API routes.

## Coding conventions

### General
- All components are Server Components by default. Add `'use client'` only
  when needed (event handlers, browser APIs, hooks with state).
- Use `async/await` throughout — no `.then()` chains.
- All DB calls go through `src/lib/supabase/` helper functions — never
  write raw Supabase queries inline in components or API routes.
- All Strava API calls go through `src/lib/strava/client.ts`.
- All Claude API calls go through `src/lib/ai/claude.ts`.

### Error handling
- API routes always return typed error responses: `{ error: string, code: string }`.
- Use try/catch on every external API call (Strava, Open-Meteo, Claude).
- Webhook endpoint must return 200 immediately before any async processing.
- Never let a webhook handler time out — acknowledge first, process async.

### TypeScript
- Define all DB types in `src/types/database.ts` — generated from Supabase
  schema where possible.
- Define all Strava API response types in `src/types/strava.ts`.
- No implicit returns in async functions — always explicitly return or throw.

### Tailwind
- Use design system CSS variables via Tailwind's arbitrary value syntax:
  `bg-[var(--surface)]`, `text-[var(--text2)]`, `border-[var(--border)]`.
- Never hardcode hex colours in className strings.
- Mobile-first — base styles for mobile, `md:` and `lg:` for larger screens.

### Run type classification
Runs are classified automatically on ingestion:
- `race` — if Strava `workout_type === 1`
- `long` — distance >= 16000m AND avg_hr < threshold_hr * 0.85
- `tempo` — avg_hr > threshold_hr * 0.88 OR avg_pace < threshold_pace * 0.95
- `easy` — everything else
When threshold_hr is unknown (settings not set), use 185 as default estimate.

### Training load (CTL/ATL/TSB)
- TSS per run = estimated from HR zones when power unavailable
- CTL = 42-day EWMA of daily TSS
- ATL = 7-day EWMA of daily TSS
- TSB = CTL - ATL
- Recompute on every new run ingested — store daily snapshots in DB

## AI features (v1 scope — all reactive, no push)
1. Training load analysis — 4-week/8-week narrative via Claude
2. Race predictor — weighted Riegel formula + Claude confidence narrative
3. Anomaly detection — z-score HR vs pace, Claude explanation
4. Weather correlation — linear regression pace vs weather, Claude summary

## What is NOT in v1 (do not implement)
- Apple Health / Apple Watch integration
- Natural language querying
- Proactive notifications or email digests
- Smart weekly plan generator
- Multi-user support
- Shoe mileage tracking

## Strava webhook security
The webhook POST endpoint must:
1. Verify `owner_id === STRAVA_OWNER_ID`
2. Verify `subscription_id === STRAVA_SUBSCRIPTION_ID`
3. Only process `object_type === 'activity'` AND `aspect_type === 'create'`
4. Return 200 immediately, process async

The webhook GET endpoint (subscription verification) must:
1. Verify `hub.verify_token === STRAVA_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN`
2. Echo back `hub.challenge`

## Git conventions
- Branch: `feature/milestone-N-description`
- Commits: conventional commits — `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`
- Every DB schema change = a new numbered migration file
- Never commit `.env.local` or any file containing secrets
